; Errors and warnings from convert name the CSV line they come from.
; The line count used to cover data rows only, so the header and any
; "#" comment lines were left out: the bad row in the first block, on
; line 5, was reported as line 2.  The second block's row has a cost
; but no amount; it still fails at finalization (now naming line 2),
; which also pins that the cost-sign rule leaves a null amount alone.

test -f /dev/null convert test/regress/csv-error-line-number.csv --account Assets:Bank -> 1
__ERROR__
While parsing file "$sourcepath/test/regress/csv-error-line-number.csv", line 5:
While parsing CSV line:
  bogus,Cafe,$5

Error: Invalid date: bogus
end test

test -f /dev/null convert test/regress/csv-cost-only.csv --account Assets:Bank -> 1
__ERROR__
While parsing file "$sourcepath/test/regress/csv-cost-only.csv", line 2:
While parsing CSV line:
  2024/01/03,Broker,,$12

Error: Cannot determine if an uninitialized amount is zero
end test
